artford and  who has been working over the past 18  months or longer longer longer than 18  months with the the Ministry of  Education in Rwanda on a project that is  redesigning how how they how the Rwandan  education system works and how the  genocide is dealt with within Rwanda as  well so first Jan then Joe thank you  so invite you if you are comfortable to  do so to pray with me if you prefer to  receive these words as words of  meditation please do that as well o God  of mercy we gather today in a season of  mourning and remembrance to honor the  victims of the genocide in Rwanda 20  years ago a terrible moment in the arc  of human history when the earth was  soaked with unspeakable violence the  heavens gasped as hand and weapon were  raised against sister and brother in a  flurry of hatred and fear your divine  heart O God was wrenched into by the  brutal murder and suffering of so many  of your children today most of us  remember the death inflicted as a number  beyond comprehension but you remember  each beloved soul by name as they  breathe their last in this moment of  silence we honor those who died and we  remember their story  in your mercy hear our prayer god of  courage we give you thanks and ask your  blessing on the survivors who so  courageously continue to tell their  story especially those whose voices  speak today may we show a similar  courage to hear these stories of  unbearable suffering so that we too  might help carry the mantle forward as  ones who vow to remember may it be their  resilience that compels our memory and  Spurs us into action in this moment of  silence we honor the survivors  especially those who continue to suffer  and we remember their story  in your mercy hear our prayers o God of  justice too often we have chosen to  ignore that we are citizens in a global  community brothers and sisters in our  humanity bind us o God with your justice  so as not to forget our moral moral  obligation to care for the other whether  near